---
description: Blank line between logical groups of related declarations; keep siblings in a group tight.
globs: "**/*.{tsx}"
alwaysApply: false
---

# Group related declarations

Separate logical groups of related variable declarations with a blank line. Keep declarations in the same group adjacent (no blank line between them).

Typical groups in React components:

- Data / query hooks
- Local state (`useState`, etc.)
- Derived values / plain consts
- Event handlers / callbacks
- Effects (already usually separated)

```tsx
// Bad — one packed block, or blank lines inside a group
const { data: isAuthenticated, isLoading } = useQueryAuthenticated()
const [isMounted, setIsMounted] = useState(false)
const [isScrolled, setIsScrolled] = useState(false)
const x = 5
const y = 10

// Good — blank line between groups; siblings stay tight
const { data: isAuthenticated, isLoading } = useQueryAuthenticated()

const [isMounted, setIsMounted] = useState(false)
const [isScrolled, setIsScrolled] = useState(false)

const x = 5
const y = 10
```

Do not insert a blank line between two declarations that belong to the same group. Prefer grouping by purpose over sorting every `const` into one list.
